# Workflow-control files (workflows, actions, CODEOWNERS, scripts workflows run with the
# automation token, the reviewer agent) are the CI/CD trust boundary — require the repo owner's review
# on any change to them, structurally enforced via branch protection
# ("Require review from Code Owners", a manual repo-settings prerequisite tracked
# in issue #62), in addition to the PR babysitter routine's no-loop rule (docs/AUTOMATION.md).
# The sole owner can't approve their own PRs: once code-owner review is required, the maintainer's
# own workflow-control PRs merge via a ruleset bypass (or a second owner added here).
